 "notes": [
  "The two images (ATmega328P memory map and the Arduino IDE Tools > Programmer menu) are not circuit diagrams; the circuit is taken from the text: Uno programmer to Uno target using the 'old style' wiring (D11 MOSI, D12 MISO, D13 SCK, D10 to target RESET, 5V, GND).",
  "The ICSP-header wiring alternative was not used; the equivalent D11-D13 pin wiring is shown.",
  "The 10 \u00b5F capacitor (POS to programmer RESET, NEG to programmer GND) is included because the programmer is an Uno; it is fitted after the ArduinoISP sketch has been uploaded.",
  "The three optional feedback LEDs follow the ArduinoISP sketch pin defaults: heartbeat D9, error D8, programming D7. The manual gives no resistor value; 220 \u03a9 resistors and the breadboard layout are assumptions.",
  "The USB cable from the programmer to the computer is not modelled; the manual says to leave boards unpowered while wiring.",
  "The target is assumed to be an Uno; the manual also shows a Nano, Mega and MKR1000 as variants, which are not built here."
 ],
